-- title:
--   Degree p⁴ for [p] on the edge-family formal 𝒪_D-module
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $\iota\colon\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})\to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $\bar k = W(k)/pW(k)$ and let $E$ be the edge chart ring `EdgeFamily.edgeRingCharP p` $\bar k$, i.e. the localisation of the edge quotient of $\bar k$ at its discriminant, taken with parameter $0$ and residue degree $p$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $E$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $E$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of $F$, additive and multiplicative in the acting element, and a uniformiser endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$ for the Witt Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $\gamma_0,\gamma_1$ be elements of the Cartier module of $F$ forming a homogeneous $V$-basis for the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}\to W(k)\to\bar k\to E$, that is, $\gamma_i$ lies in the $i$-th graded piece (each Teichmüller element $c$ of $\mathbb{F}_{p^2}$ acts on $\gamma_i$ as homothety by the $p^i$-th power of its image in $E$) and the matrix of tangent vectors $(\mathrm{tangent}(\gamma_i)_j)$ has unit determinant; and assume $\gamma$ has the edge structure constants of $\bar k$, so that for every $i$ and every $N$ the image of $\gamma_i$ under $\varpi$ equals $\sum_{m<N} V^m\bigl(a_{m,i}\cdot\gamma_{(m+i+1)\bmod 2}\bigr)$ plus $V^N h$ for some $h$, where $a_{m,0}$ and $a_{m,1}$ are the branch constants of the edge coordinates $\eta$ and $\xi$ respectively. Then for every algebraically closed field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f\colon E\to\kappa$, the $\kappa$-algebra $\kappa[[X_1,X_2]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the two coefficientwise $f$-images of the power series giving multiplication by $p$ on $X$ has $\kappa$-dimension $p^4$.
--
--   This is the fibrewise degree statement for the $p$-kernel of the special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module carried by the edge chart of the formal upper half plane: at every geometric point of the chart the kernel of $[p]$ is a scheme of degree $p^4$, as expected for a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of height $4$. It is the input used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.hasHeight_four_of_hasStructureConstants_edgeRingConstants_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.hasHeight_four_of_hasStructureConstants_edgeRingConstants_of_isAlgClosed).
